# Taster of Wares: the permission is Bot1's alone ("you may cast it") and it only widens what mana may pay (CR 609.4b): it doesn't
# waive the cost. Bot1 pays for the Taster with its Black Lotus and has no mana left, so it can't cast the exiled Lightning Bolt
# (and does not pay life for it: 20 stays 20). On turn 2 Bot2 has an Island's mana open, which would pay for the Bolt it owns, but the
# Taster's controller is Bot1, not Bot2: that cast is refused too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Taster of Wares
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: B)
Bot1.Hand.Taster of Wares.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
! Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2; Mana: short)
? Bot1.Life = 20
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
! Bot2.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)

[Expect]
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
